es"]}},{"id":"pl-en-a1-listen-2","level":"A1","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:number-time","speech":"The bus leaves at seven.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a1-listen-2","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: when does the bus leave?","answers":["At seven"],"explain":"She said: the bus leaves at seven.","options":["At six","At seven","At eight","At ten"]}},{"id":"pl-en-a1-listen-3","level":"A1","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:gist","speech":"Sorry, I can't come today. I am sick.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a1-listen-3","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: what is the problem?","answers":["She is sick"],"explain":"She said: I am sick.","options":["She is sick","She is busy","She is late","She is lost"]}},{"id":"pl-en-a1-write-1","level":"A1","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:verb-be","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a1-write-1","kind":"written","prompt":"Write only the missing word: She ___ my sister. (be)","answers":["is"],"explain":"With she, use is.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-a1-write-2","level":"A1","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:plurals","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a1-write-2","kind":"written","prompt":"Write only the plural: one child, two ___","answers":["children"],"explain":"Child has an irregular plural: children.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-a1-write-3","level":"A1","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:present-simple","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a1-write-3","kind":"written","prompt":"Write the full sentence: I / want / coffee","answers":["I want coffee"],"explain":"Statement order: I want coffee.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-1","level":"A2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:past-simple-irregular","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-1","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write the missing word: Yesterday I ___ to the market. (go)","answers":["went"],"explain":"Go is irregular in the past: went.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-2","level":"A2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:comparatives","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-2","kind":"choice","prompt":"This book is ___ than the film.","answers":["better"],"explain":"Good has an irregular comparative: better.","options":["good","better","best","more good"]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-3","level":"A2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:going-to","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-3","kind":"choice","prompt":"They ___ play football tomorrow.","answers":["are going to"],"explain":"Plans with be + going to + verb: are going to play.","options":["go to","are going to","going to","goes to"]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-4","level":"A2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:countable-uncountable","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-4","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write much or many: How ___ people came?","answers":["many"],"explain":"People is countable, so many.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-5","level":"A2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:time-expressions","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-5","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write on, in or at: The party is ___ Saturday.","answers":["on"],"explain":"Days take on: on Saturday.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-6","level":"A2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:past-continuous","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-core-6","kind":"choice","prompt":"I ___ dinner when the phone rang.","answers":["was cooking"],"explain":"An action in progress interrupted by a short one: was cooking.","options":["cooked","was cooking","am cooking","have cooked"]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-listen-1","level":"A2","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:inference","speech":"We moved here because the rents were cheaper.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-listen-1","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: why did they move?","answers":["Cheaper rents"],"explain":"She said: because the rents were cheaper.","options":["Cheaper rents","A new job","Better weather","Closer family"]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-listen-2","level":"A2","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:detail","speech":"I'll meet you outside the cinema at eight.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-listen-2","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: where will they meet?","answers":["Outside the cinema"],"explain":"She said: outside the cinema.","options":["Outside the cinema","Inside the cinema","At the bus stop","At a restaurant"]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-listen-3","level":"A2","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:detail","speech":"She's taller than her brother, but he's faster.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-listen-3","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: who is faster?","answers":["Her brother"],"explain":"She said: he's faster.","options":["Her brother","She is","Both are equal","Nobody is"]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-write-1","level":"A2","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:past-simple-irregular","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-write-1","kind":"written","prompt":"Write only the missing word: Last week she ___ a dress. (buy)","answers":["bought"],"explain":"Buy is irregular: bought.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-write-2","level":"A2","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:comparatives","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-write-2","kind":"written","prompt":"Write only the comparative of happy:","answers":["happier"],"explain":"Happy → happier (y → ier).","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-a2-write-3","level":"A2","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:going-to","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-a2-write-3","kind":"written","prompt":"Write the full sentence: they / play football / tomorrow","answers":["They are going to play football tomorrow","They're going to play football tomorrow","They are going to play football"],"explain":"Be + going to for plans: They are going to play football tomorrow.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-1","level":"B1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:present-perfect","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-1","kind":"choice","prompt":"I ___ her since 2019.","answers":["have known"],"explain":"States that continue up to now take the present perfect: have known.","options":["know","knew","have known","am knowing"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-2","level":"B1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:first-conditional","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-2","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write the missing word: If it rains, we ___ stay home. (will/can — one word)","answers":["will","can"],"explain":"First conditional: if + present, will + verb.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-3","level":"B1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:used-to","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-3","kind":"choice","prompt":"I ___ live in Rome, but I moved away.","answers":["used to"],"explain":"Past habits that stopped: used to live.","options":["use to","used to","am used to","was use to"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-4","level":"B1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:relative-clauses","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-4","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write who or which: The film ___ won the prize was French.","answers":["which","that"],"explain":"Which (or that) for things.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-5","level":"B1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:speculation","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-5","kind":"choice","prompt":"The lights are on. They ___ be home.","answers":["must"],"explain":"A logical deduction: must be.","options":["must","can't","shouldn't","needn't"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-6","level":"B1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:second-conditional","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-core-6","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write the missing word: If I ___ more time, I would travel. (have)","answers":["had"],"explain":"Second conditional: if + past, would + verb.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-listen-1","level":"B1","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:inference","speech":"If it rains tomorrow, we'll postpone the picnic.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-listen-1","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: what will they do if it rains?","answers":["Postpone the picnic"],"explain":"She said: we'll postpone the picnic.","options":["Postpone the picnic","Cancel the picnic","Have the picnic inside","Go for a walk"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-listen-2","level":"B1","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:detail","speech":"He must have forgotten about the meeting; he never showed up.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-listen-2","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: what happened?","answers":["He forgot the meeting"],"explain":"He must have forgotten = a deduction about the past.","options":["He forgot the meeting","He hates meetings","He arrived late","He cancelled the meeting"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-listen-3","level":"B1","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:connected-speech","speech":"I would've called you, but my phone died.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-listen-3","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: why didn't she call?","answers":["Her phone died"],"explain":"Would've is the contraction of would have; the reason is the phone died.","options":["Her phone died","She was busy","She had no credit","She forgot"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-write-1","level":"B1","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:second-conditional","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-write-1","kind":"written","prompt":"Write only the missing word: If I ___ more time, I would travel. (have)","answers":["had"],"explain":"Second conditional if-clause takes the past: had.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-write-2","level":"B1","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:present-perfect","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-write-2","kind":"written","prompt":"Write the full sentence: she / never / visit / Rome","answers":["She has never visited Rome","She's never visited Rome"],"explain":"Present perfect: has + never + past participle.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b1-write-3","level":"B1","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:relative-clauses","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b1-write-3","kind":"written","prompt":"Write only the missing word: The man ___ called you is my uncle.","answers":["who","that"],"explain":"Who (or that) for people.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-1","level":"B2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:passive-intro","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-1","kind":"choice","prompt":"The bridge ___ in 1932.","answers":["was built"],"explain":"Passive past simple: was + built.","options":["built","was built","has built","was building"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-2","level":"B2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:reported-speech-basic","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-2","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write the missing word: He said he ___ tired. (original: \"I am tired\")","answers":["was"],"explain":"Reported speech shifts am → was.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-3","level":"B2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:third-conditional","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-3","kind":"choice","prompt":"If I ___ known, I would have called you.","answers":["had"],"explain":"Third conditional: if + had + participle.","options":["had","have","would have","did"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-4","level":"B2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:wish-clauses","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-4","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write the missing word: I wish I ___ the answer. (know — past form)","answers":["knew"],"explain":"Wish about the present takes the past: I wish I knew.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-5","level":"B2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:phrasal-verbs","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-5","kind":"choice","prompt":"They had to ___ the meeting because of the storm.","answers":["call off"],"explain":"Call off = cancel.","options":["call off","call on","call for","call up"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-6","level":"B2","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:connectors","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-core-6","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write one word: ___ the rain, we went out. (= despite)","answers":["despite"],"explain":"Despite + noun; in spite of means the same.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-listen-1","level":"B2","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:inference","speech":"Had I known about the delay, I would have called you.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-listen-1","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: did she know about the delay?","answers":["No, she didn't"],"explain":"Had I known... is an inverted third conditional: she did NOT know.","options":["No, she didn't","Yes, she did","She isn't sure","She found out later"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-listen-2","level":"B2","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:inference","speech":"She's said to be the best lawyer in town.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-listen-2","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: what does the sentence tell us?","answers":["People say she's the best"],"explain":"X is said to be... = reporting what people say, not her own words.","options":["People say she's the best","She said she's the best","She hired a lawyer","She won a case"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-listen-3","level":"B2","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:connected-speech","speech":"The bridge was being repaired, so traffic was diverted.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-listen-3","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: why was traffic diverted?","answers":["The bridge was being repaired"],"explain":"Was being repaired = past continuous passive: the repair caused the diversion.","options":["The bridge was being repaired","There was an accident","The road was flooded","It was a holiday"]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-write-1","level":"B2","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:passive-intro","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-write-1","kind":"written","prompt":"Write the full passive sentence: they / build / the bridge / in 1932","answers":["The bridge was built in 1932"],"explain":"Passive past: was + built.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-write-2","level":"B2","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:wish-clauses","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-write-2","kind":"written","prompt":"Write only the missing word: I wish I ___ the answer. (know)","answers":["knew"],"explain":"Wish + past for a present regret: knew.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-b2-write-3","level":"B2","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:reported-speech-basic","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-b2-write-3","kind":"written","prompt":"Write the reported sentence: He said, \"I am tired.\" → He said ___","answers":["He said he was tired","He said that he was tired"],"explain":"Reported: am → was.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-1","level":"C1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:connectors","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-1","kind":"choice","prompt":"Rarely ___ such a clear explanation.","answers":["have we heard"],"explain":"A negative adverbial in front position triggers inversion: have we heard.","options":["we have heard","have we heard","we heard","did we heard"]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-2","level":"C1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:gerunds-infinitives","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-2","kind":"choice","prompt":"___ worries me is the deadline, not the workload.","answers":["What"],"explain":"A cleft sentence with What ... is ... focuses the concern.","options":["That","What","Which","It"]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-3","level":"C1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:connectors","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-3","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write one formal word meaning despite: The risk was real; ___, they proceeded.","answers":["nevertheless","nonetheless","however"],"explain":"Nevertheless/nonetheless/however all mark contrast; the sentence needs one after the semicolon.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-4","level":"C1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:modal-must-have-to","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-4","kind":"choice","prompt":"She ___ have missed the train — she left an hour early.","answers":["can't"],"explain":"Can't have + participle = a near-certain negative deduction about the past.","options":["mustn't","can't","shouldn't","wouldn't"]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-5","level":"C1","mode":"core","skill":"vocab:collocations","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-5","kind":"choice","prompt":"The report ___ light on the causes of the failure.","answers":["shed"],"explain":"Fixed collocation: shed light on something.","options":["made","gave","shed","put"]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-6","level":"C1","mode":"core","skill":"grammar:future-forms","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-core-6","kind":"gap","prompt":"Write one word: By June, she ___ have finished the thesis. (will/may — auxiliary of the future perfect)","answers":["will","may","might","could"],"explain":"Future perfect: will/may/might/could + have + participle.","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-listen-1","level":"C1","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:inference","speech":"Not only did the plan fail, but it also backfired.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-listen-1","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: what happened to the plan?","answers":["It failed and harmed them"],"explain":"Not only ... but also ...; backfired = had the opposite, harmful effect.","options":["It failed and harmed them","It only partly failed","It worked unexpectedly","It was never tried"]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-listen-2","level":"C1","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:inference","speech":"But for your help, the launch would have collapsed.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-listen-2","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: what does she mean?","answers":["Your help prevented a collapse"],"explain":"But for = if it hadn't been for: an unreal past; the help made the difference.","options":["Your help prevented a collapse","The launch collapsed anyway","You should help more","The launch was a disaster"]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-listen-3","level":"C1","mode":"listening","skill":"listening:inference","speech":"The committee's decision, however controversial, stands.","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-listen-3","kind":"choice","prompt":"Listen: what is the status of the decision?","answers":["It stands despite controversy"],"explain":"However controversial = a concession: despite the controversy, it stands.","options":["It stands despite controversy","It was reversed","It is still debated","It was never made"]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-write-1","level":"C1","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:connectors","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-write-1","kind":"written","prompt":"Write the full inverted sentence: I have rarely heard such a clear explanation. Start with: Rarely...","answers":["Rarely have I heard such a clear explanation"],"explain":"Fronted negative adverbial inverts auxiliary and subject: Rarely have I heard...","options":[]}},{"id":"pl-en-c1-write-2","level":"C1","mode":"writing","skill":"grammar:third-conditional","exercise":{"id":"pl-en-c1-write-2","kind":"written","prompt":"Complete with one word: But for th